From 519ed32dae27131ccc64770ed3c5c387563bf333 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Travis Gilbert <1travisgilbert@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:23:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gpui-web): size the window without ResizeObserver

The ResizeObserver callback was the only path that ever sized the
window. A browser without it kept the canvas's 1x1 backing store and
zero GPUI bounds, so nothing painted, including the native fallbacks a
missing capability is meant to leave working. The measurement now feeds
one apply_canvas_size, and without an observer the window measures the
canvas at creation and on every window resize.
